### Hand Carry Class: Purpose and Data Collection

- Ken clarified the sole purpose of hand carry detection: prevent GPS drift during human handling
  - When collar is hand-carried, system should treat dog as idle and freeze GPS position
  - Misclassifying hand carry as “dog moving” is acceptable; misclassifying it as “dog idle” is the failure case
- On shelf class purpose: trigger a battery-saving timeout after ~5 minutes of confirmed shelf detection
  - Very high accuracy due to distinct stillness and orientation; false positives considered near-zero
- Dinko’s model analysis: no overlap between hand carry and moving classes; 0.2 overlap between hand carry idle and on shelf (negligible)
- Dinko collecting additional hand carry data; will retrain and notify team when ready
  - Adrian’s labeling pipeline on hold for now; Dinko prefers to validate current model’s real-world generalization first before expanding data collection

